    "end": "He says he nearly died.",
    "caption": "The man on the left is the forecast.\n\nMolly: 2.8 million people, a 23-hour day, two moons, and colds that come out as weather. A sniffle is a flurry. A cough is a hard frost. Anything with a temperature closes the airport, and the forecast is mostly a list of who's poorly. Molly had a cold last week and carried on as normal, in a light flurry. Then her husband caught it.\n\nI had a sniffle on my first morning. The weather service named it after me.\n\n(On Earth, a Canadian doctor reviewed the evidence for 'man flu' in the BMJ in 2017 and concluded men may really suffer a bit more. Keith has printed it out.)\n\nIs yours a flurry or a blizzard?"
  },
